# Research Paper PDF Build Rules

Applies whenever converting a paper under `docnav/Research/papers/` to `.tex` and `.pdf` (Pandoc, `pandoc_paper_postprocess.py`, `research_paper_pdflatex.sh`).

## Mandatory: visible URLs in References (print-safe)

Hyperlink-only in-series references are **not acceptable** in a PDF-bound paper. Anchor text such as `[paper 1](url)` or `[Mil26a](url)` prints as "paper 1" with no URL. Printed PDFs, plain-text exports, and email attachments must remain usable without clicking links.

**Before running Pandoc or `pdflatex`, every in-series References entry must:**

1. Name the paper number in plain prose (`paper 1 in this series`, not only a hyperlink).
2. Include the full **File page** (blob) URL from `docnav/Research/papers/github_pdf_urls.md` as **visible plain text**.
3. Put the URL on its **own line** after the bibliographic line, wrapped in angle brackets so Pandoc emits `\url{...}`:

```
[Mil26a] Milton, J. W. *Title.* Clarity Coalition, paper 1 in this series, 2026.

<https://github.com/baardev/truevalue/blob/main/docnav/Research/papers/1_recursive-tholonic-five-constants/1_recursive-tholonic-five-constants.pdf>
```

Do **not** use hyperlink-only forms such as:

```
[Mil26a](url) Milton, J. W. *Title.* ... [paper 1](url), 2026.
```

Prose cross-references in the body may remain as `[Paper 1](url)` hyperlinks for digital reading. The References section is where print readers resolve paper numbers to sources.

## Pre-build gate (do not skip)

Before `research_paper_pdflatex.sh`:

- [ ] Every in-series References entry has a visible URL on its own line (angle-bracket form above).
- [ ] No in-series References entry relies on hyperlink anchor text alone.
- [ ] URLs match `github_pdf_urls.md` (`github.com/.../blob/main/...`, never `raw.githubusercontent.com`, never `/raw/main/`).

If any entry fails, fix the `.md` **before** building the PDF. Do not ship a PDF with hyperlink-only References.

## Post-build verification

After the PDF is generated, confirm the References pages show full URLs as readable text (not only blue "paper 1" links). Long URLs must wrap (`xurl` is included in `pandoc_paper_postprocess.py` for this).

